{"id":"r8","level":1,"levelName":"Reading","n":8,"of":9,"title":"The dot that changes the sound","titleHe":"דָּגֵשׁ","goal":"Read בּ/ב, כּ/כ, פּ/פ — and sound out whole words unaided.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"A dot inside a letter is a dagesh. In modern Hebrew it changes the sound of exactly three letters."},{"type":"dagesh","items":[{"soft":"בֿ","hard":"בּ","en":"vet → bet","sound":"v becomes b"},{"soft":"כֿ","hard":"כּ","en":"khaf → kaf","sound":"kh becomes k"},{"soft":"פֿ","hard":"פּ","en":"fe → pe","sound":"f becomes p"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"The other nineteen letters take a dagesh too, but it makes no audible difference today — so when you see one elsewhere, read straight through it."},{"type":"text","body":"That is the whole reading system: you can now sound out anything carrying vowel marks. One thing is still missing, and it is the next lesson — where in the word to put the weight."}],"vocab":[{"he":"בַּיִת","en":"house","translit":"bayit"},{"he":"כֶּלֶב","en":"dog","translit":"kelev"},{"he":"פַּעַם","en":"once, a time","translit":"pa'am"},{"he":"אוֹכֵל","en":"eats","translit":"ochel"},{"he":"סַבָּא","en":"grandfather","translit":"saba"},{"he":"מִשְׁפָּחָה","en":"family","translit":"mishpacha"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"בּ — with the dot — sounds like?","options":["p","b","k","ch as in Bach"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בּ"},{"type":"choice","q":"כּ — with the dot — sounds like?","options":["ch as in Bach","p","b","k"],"correct":3,"prompt":"כּ"},{"type":"choice","q":"פּ — with the dot — sounds like?","options":["p","k","b","ch as in Bach"],"correct":0,"prompt":"פּ"},{"type":"choice","q":"Where is the dot in shin?","options":["there is no dot","under the letter","dot on the left","dot on the right"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שׁ"},{"type":"choice","q":"Where is the dot in sin?","options":["dot on the left","under the letter","dot on the right","there is no dot"],"correct":0,"prompt":"שׂ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["question, issue","taxi","like, as","house"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בַּיִת","translit":"bayit"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["dog","revolution","a machine","accepted, customary"],"correct":0,"prompt":"כֶּלֶב","translit":"kelev"},{"type":"read","he":"פַּעַם","translit":"pa'am","en":"once, a time"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["בַּיִת","house"],["כֶּלֶב","dog"],["פַּעַם","once, a time"],["אוֹכֵל","eats"],["סַבָּא","grandfather"]]},{"type":"read","he":"אוֹכֵל","translit":"ochel","en":"eats"},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["אוֹכֵל","מִשְׁפָּחָה","סַבָּא","כֶּלֶב"],"correct":3,"say":"כֶּלֶב","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “once, a time”?","options":["אֵם","כְּגוֹן","שֶׁלִּי","פַּעַם"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"סַבָּא","translit":"saba","en":"grandfather"},{"type":"read","he":"כֶּלֶב","translit":"kelev","en":"dog"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “dog”?","options":["פִּתְאוֹם","בִּינָה","מוֹנִית","כֶּלֶב"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “grandfather” in Hebrew","answer":"סַבָּא","hint":"saba"}]}